    <h2>What is Alaska Daylight Time (AKDT)?</h2>
    <p>
      Alaska Daylight Time (AKDT) is the timezone offset used in the US state of Alaska during the summer months. It is positioned at UTC-8, making it 8 hours behind Coordinated Universal Time (UTC) and Greenwich Mean Time (GMT).
    </p>
    <p>
      AKDT is active from the second Sunday of March, when clocks spring forward from AKST, to the first Sunday of November, when clocks fall back. This daylight saving system covers the vast majority of Alaska's landmass, including major municipal and commercial centers.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
