    <div class="eyebrow">DST Rules</div>
    <h2>Daylight Saving Time in Alaska</h2>
    <p>
      Daylight Saving Time (DST) rules in Alaska match standard US guidelines. Clocks spring forward one hour on the second Sunday of March, shifting the state from standard time (AKST) to daylight saving time (AKDT). Clocks fall back one hour on the first Sunday of November, returning the state to AKST.
    </p>
    <p>
      Crucially, the United Kingdom and continental Europe change their clocks on different dates—specifically on the last Sunday of March and the last Sunday of October. This creates a two-to-three week transition window in spring and autumn where the relative offset shifts to 7 hours or 10 hours. Our database-aware calculator handles these transition anomalies seamlessly.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
