  <h2>Final Summary</h2>
  <p>
    Converting **GMT to AKDT** requires understanding the seasonal transitions of Alaska Time. During the winter, the region observes Alaska Standard Time (AKST) at a nine-hour offset (UTC-9). During the summer, it observes Alaska Daylight Time (AKDT) at an eight-hour offset (UTC-8). Utilizing a date-aware timezone converter ensures schedules are computed accurately, avoiding missed connections.
  </p>
